## Findings
1. blocking — brief:68 [severity: S1] A malformed or unreadable remote-tracking ref makes `git show-ref` exit 128/-1, but `unpushedBranches` treats every nonzero exit as `NONE`; the real done caller can therefore remove an old worktree whose branch may be pushed and have an open PR, while W-489-b4/K22 tests only present versus absent refs. Replace brief:68 with: “| 5. PR state and remote-ref evidence, as `PrLookup`, `ghPrStates`, and `unpushedBranches` read them | `PrLookup` answers `OPEN`, `MERGED`, `CLOSED`, or `NONE`; `ghPrStates` accepts its stated JSON domain; `unpushedBranches` accepts `git show-ref` exit 0 as present/unread and exit 1 as absent/`NONE` | `sweepWorktrees` keeps errors, unread states, and open PRs; `ghPrStates` rejects command or JSON failures; `unpushedBranches` returns `{ error }` for every `show-ref` result other than 0 or 1, so the sweep keeps the branch candidate |”. [design: keeps] [class: spec×input-without-named-rejector] — check: packages/cli/src/next-done.test.ts (W-489-b4: `show-ref` exit 128 keeps the worktree)
